From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pmos-laurel-sprout <dev@laurel.invalid>
Date: 2026-08-15
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sm6125: add qcom,rmtfs-mem region

Downstream-only patch for the frozen 6.1 fork at
77de535b8dbd8f483b5802c8937cb714bab5b485.

Adds the rmtfs (EFS) shared-memory region required by the qcom_rmtfs_mem
driver so that rmtfs userspace can create /dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem1 and serve
the modem EFS over QMI. Without this node rmtfs aborts in
rmtfs_mem_open(), MPSS stays offline and WCN3990 QMI WLFW never arrives
(verified in physical test v3, WIFI-V3-MPSS-RMTFS-BLOCKED).

Addressing follows the vendor SM6125/trinket sources (android_kernel_
xiaomi_sm6125, lineage-18.1 through lineage-23.2 /e/OS A16): the vendor
laurel_sprout DT defines NO static rmtfs carve-out and allocates the
region dynamically (qcom,sharedmem-uio with reg = <0x0 0x200000>, client
id 1). Hence this node uses the mainline dynamic reserved-memory form
(size + alloc-ranges, no reg), with the documented vendor size 0x200000
(2 MiB) and qcom,client-id = <1> to match /dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem1.

qcom,vmid is intentionally omitted: the 6.1 binding treats it as
optional (triggers qcom_scm_assign_mem) and no downstream laurel_sprout
source uses it for rmtfs. If a physical test shows the modem cannot reach
the region, the guard-pages backport (9265bc6bce69) or a vmid should be
re-evaluated.

Signed-off-by: pmos-laurel-sprout <dev@laurel.invalid>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi
index b71b246..fa03a2e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi
@@ -364,7 +364,16 @@
 		qseecom_ta_mem: memory@13fc00000 {
 			reg = <0x1 0x3fc00000 0x0 0x400000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		rmtfs_mem: rmtfs-mem {
+			compatible = "qcom,rmtfs-mem";
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x0 0x1 0x0>;
+			size = <0x0 0x200000>;
+			no-map;
+
+			qcom,client-id = <1>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	smem: smem {
